  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Differences**\n\nI\'ve successfully run `tsc --noEmit` and it passed without any errors! Now, I\'m shifting my focus to the visual presentation. I\'m taking a close look at `FooterSection.tsx` and the user\'s provided screenshot. Specifically, I\'m beginning by comparing the top horizontal divider within the footer section, looking for any discrepancies in appearance.\n\n\n**Defining Footer Structure**\n\nI\'ve got the footer\'s layout and content defined now: four distinct columns with specified content including \"About\", \"Quick Links\", \"Our Service\", and \"Contact Info.\" I\'ve listed the full content in each column, including the paragraph, links, contact details, and a copyright notice. I\'m focusing on the structural components now, and plan to move to style and responsive behavior.\n\n\n**Refining Component Spacing**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the finer details. I\'ve decided on `space-y-2 sm:space-y-3` for vertical rhythm between list items. The \"About\" section gets the styling I\'ve selected, with line-height and max-width (`text-neutral-600 leading-[1.6] max-w-[280px] lg:max-w-[320px]`). I\'ve also incorporated the divider line below the paragraph. Additionally, I\'ve styled the \"Social Media:\" label and the social media icons to match the screenshot precisely, ensuring the spacing and font weights are correct. I\'m focusing on these elements to make sure it looks great.\n\n\n**Verifying Responsiveness Goals**\n\nI\'m now diving into the responsive behavior of the footer. The center divider line is centered and specified as 260-320px wide. I\'ve confirmed the copyright matches the screenshot exactly. Now, I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s fully responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile. On tablet, I plan to balance between 2 or 4 column grid layouts with clear touch targets. I will ensure no awkward wrapping occurs by checking the typography on a range of devices.\n\n\n**Confirming Mobile-First Layout**\n\nI\'m now implementing the mobile-first approach. I\'ve designed a clean stacked or 2-column mobile layout. The spacing feels good, and the touch targets are all greater than or equal to 44px. I\'ve added interactive modals for Privacy, Contact, Gym Location, and Services to ensure user-friendliness on mobile. I\'ve also incorporated a \"back to top\" button. I\'m double-checking the `forcedViewport` adjustments in `FooterSection.tsx` and verifying the styling with the tablet view. I\'m focusing on text and widths for tablets.\n\n\n**Enhancing Contact Information**\n\nI\'m now implementing the detailed styling for the contact information within the footer. I\'ve focused on ensuring the labels (\"Mail:\", \"Call:\", etc.) are bold and the corresponding values use normal weight, matching the screenshot perfectly. I\'m also addressing the \"Social Media\" section by incorporating the underline above it, making sure the horizontal divider\'s style, width, and margin are exactly as depicted.\n\n\n"
